    "summary": "Alligator>Drums>Eleven blaze, soaring Easy Wind, tight China>Rider",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a ferocious Alligator‑Drums‑Eleven jam and a lyrical Easy Wind that soars above the early‑70 rawness. Highlights include a primo China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue and a strong second set with Dire Wolf, Uncle John’s Band intro and Cryptical/Drums/The Other One sequence.",
    "review": "Portland’s Springer's Inn on January 16, 1970 captures the Dead in a transitional moment where raw early‑70 energy meets growing tightness. The first set kicks off with a punchy Alligator that segues into an inspired drum duel and a blistering Eleven jam – Jerry’s guitar tone is crisp and expressive while Mickey and Bill drive the rhythm forward. Even with a few tape cuts (Cumberland Blues, part of Cosmic Charlie), the band stays cohesive, delivering spirited renditions of Dancin’ In The Street and a heartfelt Dire Wolf. The second set really shines: China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider rolls out with enthusiastic playing from Jerry, Phil lays down solid bass foundations, and the Cryptical > Drums > The Other One suite showcases the drummers at their peak. Easy Wind soars as a highlight, and Uncle John’s Band opens with an “over‑the‑top” intro that sets a high‑energy tone for the remainder of the night.",
